<title>UK: BT slides 3 percent on MCI concerns.</title>
<headline>BT slides 3 percent on MCI concerns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Telecommunications Plc continued to fall on Monday amid concerns over its planned merger with troubled U.S. telecoms group MCI Communications Corp.</p>
<p>Shares in the BT were down three percent or 13 1/2 pence to 416-1/2p in early dealing. The company's value has slid 13 percent since MCI warned on July 10 that it would lose $800 million this year through its attempts to enter the U.S. local call market.</p>
<p>BT chief executive Sir Peter Bonfield was due to fly to the U.S. on Monday to discuss the future of the planned merger.</p>
</text>
